<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#magnetic-compass">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Magnetic compass</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as compass</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The magnetic compass is a navigational instrument that uses a magnetised needle to indicate direction. It was developed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and was used for navigation at sea under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a>, among the earliest recorded uses. Its spread aided maritime trade under the Song and Yuan dynasties and later transformed navigation worldwide.</p></div>
